## Claim
Text: "President Ferdinand Marcos and Dr. Jose Rizal established and founded the WORLD BANK and International Monetary Fund."
Claim author: Bangon Bansang Maharlika
Claim date: October 22, 2020

## Initial Q&A
### In what year and at what conference was the World Bank formally established?
Answer: The World Bank was formally established at the Bretton Woods Conference, officially known as the "United Nations Monetary and Financial Conference," which convened in July 1944 at the Mount Washington Hotel in Bretton Woods, New Hampshire, with delegates from 44 nations in attendance. As the source states, "The United Nations Monetary and Financial Conference, known as the Bretton Woods conference, would result in the World Bank and the International Monetary Fund." This predates both Ferdinand Marcos (who became president in 1965) and Dr. Jose Rizal (a national hero of the Philippines who lived from 1861-1896, executed by the Spanish colonial government), neither of whom had any role in founding these institutions.

Source URL: https://www.nhpr.org/the-exchange/2019-07-08/75-years-ago-n-h-s-bretton-woods-conference-reshaped-world-economic-policy

### In what year and at what conference was the International Monetary Fund formally established?
Answer: The International Monetary Fund (IMF) was formally established at the United Nations Monetary and Financial Conference, held at Bretton Woods, New Hampshire, from July 1–22, 1944. According to the source, this conference "laid the foundations for a new financial world order with two institutional pillars: the International Monetary Fund (IMF) and the International Bank for Reconstruction and Development (IBRD)."

Source URL: https://pubdocs.worldbank.org/en/634901541019944926/70-years-prologue.pdf

### What are the birth and death years of Dr. Jose Rizal, and was he alive at the time the World Bank and IMF were established?
Answer: Dr. Jose Rizal wasborn on June 19, 1861, and was executed on December 30, 1896, at age 35. The World Bank and IMF were established in 1944 at the Bretton Woods Conference — nearly five decades after Rizal's death — meaning he was long dead by the time these institutions were founded. As the source states, "Rizal was convicted of sedition and executed on December 30, 1896, at age 35."

Source URL: https://pikaahchu.weebly.com/

### During which years did Ferdinand Marcos serve as President of the Philippines, and did this period overlap with the founding of the World Bank and IMF?
Answer: Ferdinand Marcos served as President of the Philippines from 1965 to 1986, according to the source which states he "was a Filipino politician and lawyer, president of his country from 1965 to 1986." The World Bank and the International Monetary Fund were both established in 1944 at the Bretton Woods Conference and came into existence in 1945 — well before Marcos took office. Therefore, his presidency did **not** overlap with the founding of either institution, directly contradicting the claim that he "established and founded" them. (Additionally, Dr. José Rizal, the Philippine national hero, died in 1896, decades before these institutions existed.)

Source URL: https://www.amazon.com/prime-video/actor/Ferdinand-Marcos/amzn1.dv.gti.dd9c0d4c-9b1d-4b2b-abe2-174c75f7134e/

### Who were the key individuals recognized as the founders or principal architects of the World Bank?
Answer: The key individuals recognized as the founders or principal architects of the World Bank were a trio of experts: "US Treasury Secretary Henry Morganthau, his chief economic advisor Harry Dexter White, and British economist John Maynard Keynes." They designed the World Bank and IMF at the Bretton Woods conference in July 1944, and their vision was to establish a postwar economic order based on "consensual decision-making and cooperation in the realm of trade and economic relations." Notably, this directly contradicts the claim attributing the World Bank's founding to Ferdinand Marcos and Jose Rizal, as the institution was established in 1944—decades before Marcos rose to power and nearly half a century after Rizal's death in 1896.

Source URL: https://www.brettonwoodsproject.org/2019/01/art-320747/

### Who were the key individuals recognized as the founders or principal architects of the International Monetary Fund?
Answer: According to the source, the International Monetary Fund was conceived at the Bretton Woods conference in 1944, and the two key individuals recognized as its principal architects were **John Maynard Keynes** and **Harry Dexter White**, as referenced in Benn Steil's 2013 book titled *"The battle of Bretton Woods: John Maynard Keynes, Harry Dexter White, and the making of a new world order."* Neither Ferdinand Marcos nor José Rizal had any role in founding the IMF.

Source URL: https://www.europarl.europa.eu/RegData/etudes/BRIE/2015/569014/EPRS_BRI(2015)569014_EN.pdf

### Did Ferdinand Marcos or any Filipino delegate play a role in drafting the original Articles of Agreement for the World Bank and IMF?
Answer: Based on the search result, there is no mention of Ferdinand Marcos or any Filipino delegate playing a role in drafting the original Articles of Agreement for the World Bank and IMF. The key figures credited with developing the foundational ideas and proposals were **Harry Dexter White** of the U.S. Treasury Department and **John Maynard Keynes** of the British Treasury. As the source states, "Early in World War II, John Maynard Keynes of the British Treasury and Harry Dexter White of the United States Treasury Department independently began to develop ideas about the financial order of the postwar world." Furthermore, White chaired Commission I (which dealt with the IMF) and Keynes chaired Commission II (which dealt with the IBRD/World Bank). The Philippines was a U.S. Commonwealth in 1944 and did not gain independence until 1946, and Ferdinand Marcos—born in 1917—was not a delegate at the Bretton Woods Conference.

Source URL: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bretton_Woods_Conference

### Is there any credible historical record or official document from the World Bank or IMF that lists President Ferdinand Marcos or Dr. Jose Rizal among its founders?
Answer: No. The World Bank's own official historical document indicates that the World Bank and IMF were established at the United Nations Monetary and Financial Conference (Bretton Woods Conference) in July 1944, "orchestrated by the United States and countries," with no mention whatsoever of President Ferdinand Marcos or Dr. Jose Rizal as founders. Furthermore, this is historically impossible—Dr. Jose Rizal was executed by Spanish colonial authorities in 1896, nearly 50 years before these institutions were created, and Ferdinand Marcos did not become President of the Philippines until 1965, well after the World Bank and IMF were already established.

Source URL: https://pubdocs.worldbank.org/en/634901541019944926/70-years-prologue.pdf

