The claim is thoroughly refuted by historical evidence. The World Bank and IMF were both established at the [Bretton Woods Conference in July 1944](https://www.nhpr.org/the-exchange/2019-07-08/75-years-ago-n-h-s-bretton-woods-conference-reshaped-world-economic-policy), with principal architects Harry Dexter White, John Maynard Keynes, and Henry Morgenthau ([Bretton Woods Project](https://www.brettonwoodsproject.org/2019/01/art-320747/; [European Parliament](https://www.europarl.europa.eu/RegData/etudes/BRIE/2015/569014/EPRS_BRI(2015)569014_EN.pdf)), as confirmed by the [World Bank's own official history](https://pubdocs.worldbank.org/en/634901541019944926/70-years-prologue.pdf). Dr. Jose Rizal was executed in 1896—nearly 48 years before these institutions existed—making it physically impossible for him to have founded them, while Ferdinand Marcos did not become President of the Philippines until 1965, two decades after the World Bank and IMF were already operational. The only "source" for the claim is a [conspiracy theory document on Scribd](https://www.scribd.com/document/429131830/dctvteleprompt4-4-17) with no credible historical or institutional basis.